# QUIRK: while items are moved INTO a group by insert_group (and out of a group by reorder2 / group_remove /
# ungroup) the conversion to/from pixels uses the item's own parent for the "nudge to .5 px" rule. In
# insert_group the item still belongs to the top-level scene when its transform is removed, so scale and
# position snap to half pixels once; afterwards inside the group nothing snaps. A scale that is not a
# multiple of 1/540 therefore changes slightly when the item is grouped.
source s 200 100
scene main
add main s a
add main s b
scale a 1.3337 1.3337
pos a 100.26 50.76
get a
group main g a b
echo -- stored scale of a inside the group differs from 1.3337
print a
get a
